my iPad is one of my best friends we  cuddle together on the couch when I  watch Netflix it comes to bed with me  and sleeps right beside me every night  and then we spend the morning commute  together everything is so perfect until  I have to do work when it comes to  getting stuff done it is straight for  the laptop I'm just way more productive  on here with a real keyboard and real  multitasking features the tablets  they're not taking this lying down the  new trend in tablets is to make them  more work-friendly with physical  keyboard and better productivity  software the new Galaxy Tab even has a  12 inch screen to make it similar size  to a laptop but can any of these  actually make working on a tablet and  enjoyable experience  well for the last week I completely  ditched my laptop and try four of these  tablets to see how they stack up the  first one that brand new Samsung Galaxy  Note pro 750 dollar tablet has a huge  high-resolution 12 point 2 inch screen  comes with a stylus and you can buy a  keyboard cover for $99 it runs Android  but Samsung has added a lot of its own  features then I used to Windows 8.1  tablets because Microsoft confusingly  still has two Windows operating systems  the Nokia Lumia 2520 has a 10.1 inch  screen and runs Windows RT which cannot  run older Windows programs it costs 399  dollars but the keyboard which has a  battery inside costs 150 dollars more  then there is the surface pro which runs  the full version of Windows 8.1 the  tablet starts at $900 and the keyboard  with real keys cost another 130 dollars  and it currently about the tablet use  the most the iPad the $499 iPad air  doesn't have a keyboard made especially  for it so I paired it with a $99  Logitech ultrathin keyboard cover then  it was business kind  and compared all the tablets on four  pieces of criteria multitasking app  selection text input and battery life  when it comes to working multiple  programs at once in this case email  Twitter and a browser the Galaxy Note  pro actually has some good tricks some  apps can be minimized and moved around  and you can just draw a box where you  want to open a new app it sure beats the  iPad which has no way of putting two  apps next to each other but I still  found both Windows tablets to be the  best on managing apps it did the best  job of allowing me to put apps  side-by-side easily get to other open  apps and all those handy windows  keyboard tricks still work and both the  nokia and the surface have trackpad if  you don't want to reach up and touch the  screen typing tag it was a tie for the  best keyboard I was able to type  eighty-two words per minute on the  Samsung keyboard and on the surface type  cover that's that I enjoyed typing more  on the surface keyboard it's just made  better and feels nicer I typed 80 words  per minute on the nokia keyboard and  then 72 on the iPad keyboard still both  are much faster than I can type on  screen I should also mention that  there's a reason they call laptops  laptops none of these tablets like  sitting on my lap and even if you can  multitask and type fast it's not going  to matter if you have the apps you need  if you just use a browser and email then  these are all pretty evenly matched and  each of them also comes with a suite of  productivity software Samsung even  teamed up with a Korean company named  hand comb to preload software that looks  exactly like Microsoft Office hmm looks  pretty pretty similar Apple also  includes I work with any new iPad  purchase however most businesses still  use Windows programs including Word  Excel and PowerPoint that's why the  surface pro comes the closest to being a  great laptop replacement well until you  realize that the battery life seriously  takes a hit the iPad Galaxy Note pro and  Nokia were able to stream video for over  eight hours but the  purpose could only keep up for five and  a half hours is it the weekend yet as we  might have expected the Windows tablets  were the best of doing work though  Samsung didn't do a bad job especially  with multitasking that said I still  prefer my laptop I'm just more efficient  on it and then the closer these things  get it being good for work the worse  they are doing tablet II things I want  something that I can just keep on my lap  and isn't cramped and then something I  can lean back with and read and watch a  movie on which means I'm back to the  beginning I'm spending my days with my  laptop and the nights with my iPad
 

